Exp-10b :Functional interface

Aim: To write a Java program to demonstrate a functional interface.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Create a functional interface named Message.
3. Declare one abstract method called display().
4. Create a class that implements the interface.
5. Define the display method.
6. Create an object of the class.
7. Call the display method.
8. Stop the program.

Program:
@FunctionalInterface
interface Message {
    void display();
}

class Greeting implements Message {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Welcome to Java");
    }
}

public class FunctionalInterfaceExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Greeting g = new Greeting();
        g.display();
    }
}


Output:
Welcome to Java


Result: Thus, the Java program to demonstrate a functional interface was executed successfully.
